WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.501
You may not recognize Terry Gene Bollea by
his real name, but you may recognize him by

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:06.521
his wrestling name.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.620
“Ladies and gentleman...Hulk Hogan!”

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:14.690
The Hulkster became a fixture of American
pop culture thanks to the popularity of the

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:19.359
WWF, which also opened the door to his brief
career in Hollywood.

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:23.461
Unfortunately, Hollywood isn't really calling
Hogan like it did a few decades ago, thanks

00:00:23.461 --> 00:00:28.900
to a lengthy list of controversies and complications
standing between Hogan and his glory days.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.029
Here's why Hollywood won't cast Hulk Hogan
anymore.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:33.029
Hogan exposed

00:00:33.029 --> 00:00:38.290
Childhoods everywhere were ruined when Gawker
broke the story of a sex tape involving Hogan

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:43.520
and Playboy playmate Heather Cole, the wife
of Hogan's friend, Bubba "The Love Sponge"

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.610
Clem. Cole would later testify that Hogan
was just one of the many men her husband pressured

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:54.860
her into sleeping with, although she insisted
she had no idea Clem was filming the encounter.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.829
In a now infamous twist, however, the leaked
tape would prove to be the undoing of Gawker

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:00.940
itself.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:05.530
Hogan filed a lawsuit against the news site,
which was ordered to pay Hogan $31 million

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.090
in damages and subsequently forced to shut
down in 2016.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:13.220
“He was willing to do whatever it took to
take down Gawker.”

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:18.650
“I knew we were doing what was right, and
even if we would have lost...even if we would

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:21.930
have lost, it would have been good because
everybody would have known what Gawker was

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:22.930
all about.”

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:27.240
The situation is almost bizarre enough to
warrant a "based on a true story" Hollywood

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.369
movie...but even Hogan's own true story probably
wouldn't cast him anymore.

00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:33.490
“Lemme tell ya something sister brother.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:38.250
You’re gonna feel the tender embrace of
Hulkamania!”

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.540
Racist remarks

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:45.079
In case you missed it, Hulk Hogan was officially
fired by the WWE in 2015.

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:51.140
Although some said he voluntarily resigned,
the WWE insisted it fired Hogan after a series

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:56.909
of racist comments he made were secretly recorded
in yet another leaked sex tape with Heather

00:01:56.909 --> 00:01:57.909
Cole.

00:01:57.909 --> 00:02:01.980
“I mean, I am a racist, to a point, f------
n------.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.159
But then when it comes to nice people and
s---, and whatever.”

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:10.149
Hogan made a public apology for his statements,
claiming his statements didn't represent his

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:11.470
personal beliefs.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.030
In a bid to distance itself from Hogan, all
mentions of him were scrubbed from the official

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.660
WWE website and online Hall of Fame.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:23.349
Kind of a weird choice; it's not like everyone
would suddenly forget he was a major wrestling

00:02:23.349 --> 00:02:24.349
star for decades.

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:28.870
Not long after, rumors began to circulate
that the WWE might be willing to bring the

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:32.190
wrestling legend back into the fold, scandals
and all.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.160
Not so 'Hollywood'

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:39.129
Hulk's work in Hollywood, despite literally
calling himself "Hollywood" Hulk Hogan, isn't

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:40.780
exactly impressive.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:44.920
His first movie appearance was a cameo in
Rocky III as a wrestler named "Thunderlips."

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:49.190
“Thunderlips is here in the flesh, babeh!”

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:53.510
Several years later, Hogan would make his
star debut in the cult classic No Holds Barred

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:59.000
as a popular wrestler named Rip, which was
not a dramatic stretch in any way.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.740
No other wrestler had made quite as big a
splash on the big screen as Hogan…except

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:06.630
for maybe Andre the Giant…and Roddy Piper.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:12.600
“I have come here to chew bubblegum and
kick ass…

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.200
...and I’m all out of bubblegum.”

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.540
Hulk still had a few more movies than most,
and a TV series called Thunder In Paradise

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.849
to his credit.

00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:28.769
That well went dry by the late '90s, with
Hulk Hogan's last major role coming by way

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:31.550
of The Ultimate Weapon in 1998.

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:36.549
That level of cheesy action movie fare didn't
really survive through the early 2000s, leaving

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.089
Hulk out in the cold.

00:03:38.089 --> 00:03:40.129
"NOOOOOOOOOO!"

00:03:40.459 --> 00:03:42.120
A little too real

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.709
Hulk Hogan's attempts at nepotism also fell
horribly flat.

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:49.610
First, there was the attempt to use his fame
to help his daughter Brooke launch a singing

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:50.610
career.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:54.940
While she did have a few minor hits, Brooke
made the mistake of being one too many generic

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:59.910
blonde pop singers during the early 2000s,
and having a famous dad named Hulk Hogan still

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.629
wasn't enough to stand out.

00:04:01.629 --> 00:04:05.610
If that weren't enough, Hogan decided to follow
in the footsteps of The Osbournes, and put

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:08.590
his questionable family on reality TV.

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:11.520
Hogan Knows Best began airing in 2005.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.660
Although the show was semi-popular with wrestling
fans, the decision to put his family in the

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.900
spotlight created unnecessary strain for everyone
involved.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:24.530
In August 2007, Hulk's son, Nick, was involved
in a horrific car accident, and his best friend

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.150
John Graziano was severely injured.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.870
Graziano was left with permanent brain damage
and will reportedly spend the rest of his

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.970
life "in a semi-conscious state."

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:36.830
The Graziano family sued the Hogans, and the
two families settled out of court, while Nick

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.780
spent just eight months in jail.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.930
A messy divorce

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:45.830
In the immediate aftermath of Nick's car crash,
Hulk Hogan was left reeling when his wife,

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.330
Linda, filed for divorce.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:51.330
By the time the dust of the bitter divorce
settled, Linda managed to leave her marriage

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:54.000
with about 70 percent of Hulk Hogan's wealth.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.900
Linda later blamed the divorce entirely on
her ex, claiming she divorced him after he'd

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.710
had an affair with one of their daughter's
friends.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:05.910
She even went as far as to claim Hulk Hogan
had an intimate relationship with wrestler

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:09.449
Brutus Beefcake, although she later retracted
those claims.

00:05:09.449 --> 00:05:13.560
By 2008, Hogan Knows Best was cancelled, and
Hulk was devastated.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:17.620
Needless to say, the wreck of his personal
life has kept him fairly busy off-screen.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:21.610
At least he has his Pastamania money to fall
back on, right?

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:27.430
“I’ve eaten so many Hulkaroos, and Hulky-oos,
I kinda feel sorry for Big Bubba, brother!”

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.030
Can Hulk return to Hollywood?

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:33.970
Given the negative press that Hulk Hogan has
experienced in recent years, it only makes

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:38.650
sense that if he were welcomed back into the
WWE, it would be as a bad guy.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:43.729
It's certainly easier to have everyone hate
a sex-taped closet racist than to realistically

00:05:43.729 --> 00:05:45.730
turn such a guy like that into a hero.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:46.800
But who knows?

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:51.051
A successful return to the WWE could help
open a backdoor that would help Hulk Hogan

00:05:51.051 --> 00:05:52.950
ease his way back into Hollywood.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.230
It won't be easy, but it's not entirely impossible.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:59.880
Stallone, the man who helped bring Hogan into
Hollywood via that Rocky cameo, has helped

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.449
himself and other Hollywood action-movie hasbeens
stay kinda relevant thanks to his Expendables

00:06:04.449 --> 00:06:05.449
movies.

00:06:05.449 --> 00:06:07.710
Maybe a future project could make room for
Hogan?

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:11.830
Whatever moves Hulk Hogan makes to re-ignite
his Hollywood career, he'll have to be careful.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:15.390
He should know better than anyone: the cameras
are always rolling.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:20.340
Hopefully he can keep a lid on his racist
rants — and what's in his pants.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:21.340
Thanks for watching!

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:23.920
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.020
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

